# Complete Maize DRL Benchmark

A Windows-first, research-grade benchmark of **PPO, CrossQ, DSAC-T and DreamerV3** for adaptive maize irrigation in AquaCrop. It turns the earlier single-seed prototype into a controlled honours-level experiment with five evidence-based scenarios, held-out seasons, multiple seeds, equal environment-interaction budgets, statistical testing, compute accounting and non-learning baselines.

## What is compared

| Algorithm | Paradigm | Primary Windows backend |
|---|---|---|
| PPO | on-policy | Stable-Baselines3 |
| CrossQ | off-policy | SB3-Contrib implementation of the ICLR 2024 method |
| DSAC-T | distributional off-policy | native PyTorch implementation following the official DSAC-v2 equations |
| DreamerV3 | model-based world model | Ray RLlib in a separate Python environment |

The supplied official repositories are cloned into `external/`, and their exact commits are recorded. The official Danijar DreamerV3 JAX code remains an optional WSL2/Linux replication track because its repository states Linux/Mac and Python 3.11+ support.

## Five scenarios

The names match the project design and attached folder structure:

- `normal`: 35th–65th percentiles of historical seasonal precipitation;
- `dry`: 15th–35th percentiles;
- `extreme_dry`: lowest 15%;
- `limited_water`: normal-climate years with a 70% reference-irrigation allocation;
- `wet`: highest 20%.

The recent literature supports the need to test ordinary variability, drought severity, explicit water restriction and wet/waterlogging risk. The exact percentiles are transparent benchmark choices, not claims copied from the articles. See `docs/SCENARIO_EVIDENCE.md`.

## Fair primary protocol

- five seeds: `11, 23, 37, 53, 71`;
- 512,000 target real AquaCrop environment steps per algorithm × scenario × seed;
- deterministic train/validation/test year split;
- one deterministic rollout per held-out seed-year, with inferential tests performed on year-averaged independent seeds;
- same 26 observations, fixed scaling, normalized `[-1,1]` policy action (mapped to `[0,25]` mm) and reward;
- no tuning on final test years;
- paired Friedman and Wilcoxon-Holm analysis on year-averaged training seeds;
- yield–irrigation Pareto-frequency reporting on detailed seed-year rows;
- one deterministic evaluation per scenario for each non-learning baseline, avoiding pseudo-replication;
- wall-clock, memory, hardware, package and upstream-commit manifests.

The source environment uses a binary `0/25 mm` action, while CrossQ and DSAC-T require continuous Box actions and RLlib DreamerV3 assumes a tanh-centred continuous action domain. The primary comparison therefore gives **all four agents** the same normalized `[-1,1]` action, mapped linearly and identically to `0–25 mm` irrigation depth. The original binary action remains a preregistered ablation.

## Windows setup

Open PowerShell in the project folder:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned
.\scripts\bootstrap_windows.ps1
.\scripts\bootstrap_dreamer_windows.ps1
```

The base script clones all four supplied repositories, creates `.venv` with Python 3.10, installs the AquaCrop/SB3 stack, creates scenario manifests, calibrates the limited-water caps and validates the setup. DreamerV3 uses `.venv_dreamer` with Python 3.11 because its Ray/TensorFlow dependencies are isolated from the base stack.

Run a pipeline smoke test:

```powershell
.\scripts\run_benchmark.ps1 -Preset smoke
```

Run the final experiment:

```powershell
.\scripts\run_benchmark.ps1 -Preset honours -SkipExisting
```

The honours preset is large: 4 algorithms × 5 scenarios × 5 seeds. The smoke preset confirms functionality only and must not be used for final rankings. It writes to `outputs_smoke/`; the honours preset writes to `outputs/`, so a successful smoke run can never be mistaken for a final run.

## Useful single-run commands

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\train.py --algorithm ppo --scenario dry --seed 11 --timesteps 512000
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\evaluate.py --algorithm ppo --scenario dry --seed 11

.\.venv_dreamer\Scripts\python.exe scripts\train.py --algorithm dreamerv3 --scenario dry --seed 11 --timesteps 512000
.\.venv_dreamer\Scripts\python.exe scripts\evaluate.py --algorithm dreamerv3 --scenario dry --seed 11

.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts\generate_report.py
```

## Outputs

```text
outputs/
  runs/<algorithm>/<scenario>/seed_<seed>/
  evaluations/all_evaluation_rows.csv
  evaluations/primary_seed_year_rows.csv
  evaluations/primary_seed_aggregate_rows.csv
  summaries/algorithm_scenario_summary.csv
  summaries/learning_efficiency_summary.csv
  summaries/compute_summary.csv
  summaries/interaction_budget_summary.csv
  summaries/run_completeness.csv
  statistics/friedman_tests.csv
  statistics/pairwise_wilcoxon_holm.csv
  statistics/yield_water_pareto_frequency.csv
  figures/*.png
  manifests/execution_plan.json
  manifests/completion_status.json
  manifests/*.json
```

Every trained run stores its resolved configuration, package/hardware manifest, model, training log, evaluation rows, compute record and actual-versus-target interaction budget. Reporting also writes a cell-by-cell completeness audit so missing years, missing seeds or stale smoke-budget runs cannot disappear silently.

## Main metrics

Agronomic/economic: dry yield, irrigation, irrigation water productivity, profit, cumulative stress, stress days and maximum daily stress.

Learning/compute: episode reward, reward-curve AUC against real environment steps, final rolling reward, wall-clock time and peak main-process and process-tree resident memory.

The report does not collapse these into an arbitrary single score. It shows trade-offs and Pareto efficiency.

## Project map

```text
configs/          frozen benchmark, algorithm and scenario settings
docs/             experimental protocol, evidence, fairness and reporting guidance
scenarios/        generated train/validation/test manifests
scripts/          setup, training, evaluation and reporting entry points
src/maize_benchmark/
  envs/           common AquaCrop environment and wrappers
  algorithms/     PPO/CrossQ runners, full DSAC-T, DreamerV3 runner
  baselines/      rainfed, soil-moisture and fixed-interval policies
  reporting/      aggregation, statistics and figures
tests/            unit and smoke tests
```

## Scientific status

No fabricated final result is bundled. The uploaded prototype's 3000-step, one-seed results remain preliminary and are not reused as final evidence. This package supplies the complete experiment and reporting pipeline; final rankings are created only from genuine multi-seed runs on the target machine.
